  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK-Ghana Forest Governance Partnership (FGP) Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UK-Ghana Forest Partnership is the UK&apos;s latest investment into Ghana to tackle illegal and unsustainable commodity production and trade. The programme will:&gt; Work with the Forestry Commission to enhance the credibility of Ghana&#x2019;s forest governance framework and management to create stronger incentives for responsible forest management practices.&gt; Support the Forestry Commission to stop illegal mining in forest reserves and improve policy and regulations.&gt; Establish a grant mechanism to strengthen the voice + capacity of non-government stakeholders, including traditional authorities, forest-based community organisations, and independent media.</narrative>
  </description>
